 after work still report long waits. The manager said that the paper list would be placed beside the door. Leila would prefer a longer trial before making the system permanent. She has asked whether the results can be reviewed after four weeks, using both waiting times and comments from residents.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"How long has Leila lived in the building?"},{"number":2,"question":"Why was a paper list proposed?"},{"number":3,"question":"What had the caretaker discovered?"},{"number":4,"question":"Where will the paper list be placed?"},{"number":5,"question":"What two kinds of evidence should the review use?"}]},"D":{"title":"D. Listening","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the questions for one minute. Your coach will read the passage live twice. Write short answers. Each question is worth 4 marks.","delivery":"coach-live","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"When did testing begin?"},{"number":2,"question":"What has been rewritten?"},{"number":3,"question":"Does a request confirm an appointment?"},{"number":4,"question":"What should people with a reference number avoid?"},{"number":5,"question":"What feedback is specifically requested?"}]},"E":{"title":"E. Writing","marks":20,"instruction":"Write a request to the manager of a shared building. Describe a problem that has continued for some time, explain what has already been tried, propose a practical improvement and ask politely when it can be reviewed.","wordMin":110,"wordMax":140,"rubric":[{"criterion":"Task completion and relevant detail","marks":5},{"criterion":"Organisation and connection","marks":5},{"criterion":"Vocabulary appropriate to purpose","marks":5},{"criterion":"Grammar and written accuracy","marks":5}]}}},"4":{"version":3,"level":4,"title":"General English \u2014 Level 4","durationMinutes":45,"totalMarks":100,"sourceFile":"Speak_Boldly_GE_4_Exam.pdf","instructions":"Work independently without a dictionary or coursebooks. Read each instruction carefully. This is a course achievement exam; it does not certify a CEFR level. Speaking is assessed separately by your instructor. All cases are fictional.","sections":{"A":{"title":"A. Vocabulary in meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose a word from the word bank for each definition. Use each word once. Each item is worth 2 marks.","wordBank":["requirement","assumption","evidence","dependency","transition","accessible","routine","qualification","proposal","sequence"],"questions":[{"number":1,"question":"a change from one situation to another"},{"number":2,"question":"information used to support a claim"},{"number":3,"question":"a suggested plan"},{"number":4,"question":"a regular way of doing things"},{"number":5,"question":"something that is needed or expected"},{"number":6,"question":"the order in which things happen"},{"number":7,"question":"something that relies on another condition"},{"number":8,"question":"a recognised record of study or skill"},{"number":9,"question":"something accepted without checking"},{"number":10,"question":"easy for people to reach or use"}]},"B":{"title":"B. Grammar and intended meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose the correct option. Where a meaning is specified, choose the form that expresses that meaning. Each item is worth 2 marks.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"If access were easier, more people ___ attend.","options":["would","will"]},{"number":2,"question":"She ___ be at work; I am not certain. (possibility)","options":["might","must"]},{"number":3,"question":"___ the room is larger, access is harder.","options":["Although","Despite"]},{"number":4,"question":"I am used to ___ early.","options":["arrive","arriving"]},{"number":5,"question":"The manager, ___ joined years ago, agreed.","options":["who","which"]},{"number":6,"question":"He said that the meeting ___ postponed.","options":["was","has"]},{"number":7,"question":"By Friday, we will have ___ the trial.","options":["finish","finished"]},{"number":8,"question":"If she had known, she would have ___.","options":["help","helped"]},{"number":9,"question":"We should have ___ the entrance.","options":["check","checked"]},{"number":10,"question":"We had the system ___.","options":["check","checked"]}]},"C":{"title":"C. Reading","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the passage and answer using evidence from the text. Each question is worth 4 marks.","passage":"The community centre is considering moving its evening classes to a larger building. The new site has better equipment but is farther from the bus stop. A planning note says that the move must be popular because online comments are mostly positive. A volunteer challenges that inference: the comments come from people who chose to reply, and attendance records have not been examined. She acknowledges that the equipment would be useful, while arguing that access deserves a separate check. The manager, who has worked at the centre for nine years, proposes a four-week trial. By the end of the trial, the team will have compared attendance at both sites. One tutor says the old timetable should have been reviewed earlier. However, the group does not assume that an earlier review would necessarily have prevented the current difficulty. The final decision remains open pending the trial and transport information.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"What benefit and drawback does the new site have?"},{"number":2,"question":"Why are positive comments insufficient to establish popularity?"},{"number":3,"question":"What does the volunteer concede?"},{"number":4,"question":"What will the team have compared by the end of the trial?"},{"number":5,"question":"Which two sources of information will inform the final decision?"}]},"D":{"title":"D. Listening","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the questions for one minute. Your coach will read the passage live twice. Write short answers. Each question is worth 4 marks.","delivery":"coach-live","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"What did the tutor actually recommend?"},{"number":2,"question":"What will be checked before the trial?"},{"number":3,"question":"What drawback does the new room have?"},{"number":4,"question":"Does earlier transport information guarantee a different decision?"},{"number":5,"question":"When should comments reach the organiser?"}]},"E":{"title":"E. Writing","marks":20,"instruction":"Write a recommendation about moving the classes described in the reading. Compare the benefits and limits, acknowledge one valid opposing point, distinguish evidence from inference and propose a reviewable next step.","wordMin":150,"wordMax":180,"rubric":[{"criterion":"Task completion and relevant detail","marks":5},{"criterion":"Organisation and connection","marks":5},{"criterion":"Vocabulary appropriate to purpose","marks":5},{"criterion":"Grammar and written accuracy","marks":5}]}}},"5":{"version":3,"level":5,"title":"General English \u2014 Level 5","durationMinutes":45,"totalMarks":100,"sourceFile":"Speak_Boldly_GE_5_Exam.pdf","instructions":"Work independently without a dictionary or coursebooks. Read each instruction carefully. This is a course achievement exam; it does not certify a CEFR level. Speaking is assessed separately by your instructor. All cases are fictional.","sections":{"A":{"title":"A. Vocabulary in meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose a word from the word bank for each definition. Use each word once. Each item is worth 2 marks.","wordBank":["inclusive","warranty","maintenance","rationale","forecast","recollection","respondent","likelihood","viewpoint","emphasis"],"questions":[{"number":1,"question":"an estimate of a future result"},{"number":2,"question":"work that keeps something in good condition"},{"number":3,"question":"the position from which a story is told"},{"number":4,"question":"a person who answers a survey"},{"number":5,"question":"designed to involve different people"},{"number":6,"question":"special attention given to something"},{"number":7,"question":"the reason supporting a decision"},{"number":8,"question":"the chance that something will happen"},{"number":9,"question":"a promise about repair or replacement under stated terms"},{"number":10,"question":"a remembered account of something"}]},"B":{"title":"B. Grammar and intended meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose the correct option. Where a meaning is specified, choose the form that expresses that meaning. Each item is worth 2 marks.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"If the hours had not changed, the comparison ___ be clearer now.","options":["would","will"]},{"number":2,"question":"The system appears ___ help some users.","options":["to","for"]},{"number":3,"question":"Earlier, she had ___ away.","options":["move","moved"]},{"number":4,"question":"Each respondent ___ one form. (past)","options":["completed","complete"]},{"number":5,"question":"Having ___ the survey, she revised the claim.","options":["read","reading"]},{"number":6,"question":"What matters ___ the missing group.","options":["is","are"]},{"number":7,"question":"The team requested an ___ of the issue.","options":["explain","explanation"]},{"number":8,"question":"They should have ___ unsuccessful users.","options":["include","included"]},{"number":9,"question":"The finding is limited ___ the respondents.","options":["to","at"]},{"number":10,"question":"Four people had difficulty. These ___ matter.","options":["responses","response"]}]},"C":{"title":"C. Reading","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the passage and answer using evidence from the text. Each question is worth 4 marks.","passage":"A local reading room reports that its new booking system has improved access. The evidence is a survey of sixteen volunteers, twelve of whom say that booking is easier. The remaining four report difficulty finding a suitable time. The survey does not include people who stopped trying to book. A reviewer accepts that the responses describe these volunteers\u2019 experience, but questions the headline \u201cAccess improved for everyone.\u201d She also notes that longer opening hours began in the same month. The records do not separate the effects of the system from the effect of those hours. A revised report names the respondents, describes the four difficulties and avoids claiming a single cause. Having examined the survey, the reviewer recommends collecting information from unsuccessful applicants. What the report needs is a clearer account of who is missing, rather than a more confident adjective. The team agrees to retain the positive responses while narrowing the conclusion.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"How many volunteers reported easier booking?"},{"number":2,"question":"Which group is missing from the survey?"},{"number":3,"question":"Which simultaneous change complicates a causal claim?"},{"number":4,"question":"What does the reviewer accept?"},{"number":5,"question":"What additional information is recommended?"}]},"D":{"title":"D. Listening","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the questions for one minute. Your coach will read the passage live twice. Write short answers. Each question is worth 4 marks.","delivery":"coach-live","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"When had the writer used the reading room regularly?"},{"number":2,"question":"Which overbroad statement is revised?"},{"number":3,"question":"Who helped her?"},{"number":4,"question":"Why is the feeling of exclusion retained?"},{"number":5,"question":"What practical change is suggested?"}]},"E":{"title":"E. Writing","marks":20,"instruction":"Write an evaluation of the reading-room report. State what the survey supports, explain two limits, discuss an alternative explanation and make one justified recommendation. Keep the scope of every claim clear.","wordMin":180,"wordMax":210,"rubric":[{"criterion":"Task completion and relevant detail","marks":5},{"criterion":"Organisation and connection","marks":5},{"criterion":"Vocabulary appropriate to purpose","marks":5},{"criterion":"Grammar and written accuracy","marks":5}]}}},"6":{"version":3,"level":6,"title":"General English \u2014 Level 6","durationMinutes":45,"totalMarks":100,"sourceFile":"Speak_Boldly_GE_6_Exam.pdf","instructions":"Work independently without a dictionary or coursebooks. Read each instruction carefully. This is a course achievement exam; it does not certify a CEFR level. Speaking is assessed separately by your instructor. All cases are fictional.","sections":{"A":{"title":"A. Vocabulary in meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose a word from the word bank for each definition. Use each word once. Each item is worth 2 marks.","wordBank":["consent","method","causation","polarisation","premise","tradition","principle","inference","identity","attribution"],"questions":[{"number":1,"question":"a starting statement supporting an argument"},{"number":2,"question":"a relationship in which one factor produces another"},{"number":3,"question":"a sense of who a person or group is"},{"number":4,"question":"a general belief guiding decisions"},{"number":5,"question":"agreement given with relevant understanding"},{"number":6,"question":"identification of whose idea is being presented"},{"number":7,"question":"movement towards strongly opposed positions"},{"number":8,"question":"a conclusion drawn from information"},{"number":9,"question":"the procedure used to investigate"},{"number":10,"question":"a practice passed between generations"}]},"B":{"title":"B. Grammar and intended meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose the correct option. Where a meaning is specified, choose the form that expresses that meaning. Each item is worth 2 marks.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"Only after checking ___ she notice the problem. (past simple inversion)","options":["did","had"]},{"number":2,"question":"The label may ___ reduced confusion.","options":["have","has"]},{"number":3,"question":"Having ___ the interface, she wrote a report.","options":["examine","examined"]},{"number":4,"question":"They recommend that the setting ___ visible.","options":["be","being"]},{"number":5,"question":"The evidence applies ___ this trial.","options":["to","at"]},{"number":6,"question":"The reviewer is said ___ support clearer labels.","options":["to","for"]},{"number":7,"question":"Even ___ a default helps, alternatives still matter. (hypothetical)","options":["if","despite"]},{"number":8,"question":"This ___ needs explanation.","options":["finding","they"]},{"number":9,"question":"The report requests greater ___.","options":["visible","visibility"]},{"number":10,"question":"She can change it, and so ___ I.","options":["can","do"]}]},"C":{"title":"C. Reading","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the passage and answer using evidence from the text. Each question is worth 4 marks.","passage":"A neighbourhood archive introduces an online catalogue and describes it as giving visitors complete control over their searches. The default display ranks results by an unexplained rule, and changing that order requires opening a separate menu. A reviewer argues that a choice can exist without being easy to notice. Only after examining the interface did she question the phrase complete control. She does not claim that all defaults are harmful: a starting arrangement can help new users. Her recommendation is that the active setting be visible and that the alternative be explained beside it. A small trial records fewer requests for help after a label is added, but the trial also coincides with extra staff support. The conclusion therefore distinguishes observed change from its uncertain cause. The archive\u2019s summary attributes the recommendation to the reviewer rather than presenting it as the unanimous view of visitors. A further comparison is proposed before any broader claim about independent searching.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"Why might an available choice still be difficult to use?"},{"number":2,"question":"What benefit of defaults does the reviewer acknowledge?"},{"number":3,"question":"What two changes does she recommend?"},{"number":4,"question":"What complicates the causal interpretation of fewer help requests?"},{"number":5,"question":"Why is attribution important in the summary?"}]},"D":{"title":"D. Listening","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the questions for one minute. Your coach will read the passage live twice. Write short answers. Each question is worth 4 marks.","delivery":"coach-live","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"What did the earlier version claim?"},{"number":2,"question":"What distinction does the revision make?"},{"number":3,"question":"Was the alternative still available?"},{"number":4,"question":"Which preference does the group acknowledge?"},{"number":5,"question":"What must remain clear in a non-endorsing summary?"}]},"E":{"title":"E. Writing","marks":20,"instruction":"Write a critical summary of the archive case. Attribute the recommendation, acknowledge a benefit of defaults, evaluate the trial\u2019s limit and propose wording that preserves both choice and uncertainty.","wordMin":200,"wordMax":230,"rubric":[{"criterion":"Task completion and relevant detail","marks":5},{"criterion":"Organisation and connection","marks":5},{"criterion":"Vocabulary appropriate to purpose","marks":5},{"criterion":"Grammar and written accuracy","marks":5}]}}},"7":{"version":3,"level":7,"title":"General English \u2014 Level 7","durationMinutes":45,"totalMarks":100,"sourceFile":"Speak_Boldly_GE_7_Exam.pdf","instructions":"Work independently without a dictionary or coursebooks. Read each instruction carefully. This is a course achievement exam; it does not certify a CEFR level. Speaking is assessed separately by your instructor. All cases are fictional.","sections":{"A":{"title":"A. Vocabulary in meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose a word from the word bank for each definition. Use each word once. Each item is worth 2 marks.","wordBank":["focalisation","representation","stereotype","reversible","epistemic","rhetoric","hypothesis","provisional","agent","procedure"],"questions":[{"number":1,"question":"connected with knowledge and certainty"},{"number":2,"question":"an oversimplified belief about a group"},{"number":3,"question":"the person or thing performing an action"},{"number":4,"question":"a proposed explanation to be tested"},{"number":5,"question":"the perspective through which events are perceived"},{"number":6,"question":"an established sequence of actions"},{"number":7,"question":"able to be undone"},{"number":8,"question":"subject to further change or checking"},{"number":9,"question":"the way people or ideas are portrayed"},{"number":10,"question":"language chosen to influence an audience"}]},"B":{"title":"B. Grammar and intended meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose the correct option. Where a meaning is specified, choose the form that expresses that meaning. Each item is worth 2 marks.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"The interviews are said ___ describe experience.","options":["to","for"]},{"number":2,"question":"The review involves checking, comparing and ___.","options":["recording","records"]},{"number":3,"question":"Publication requires clear ___.","options":["accountable","accountability"]},{"number":4,"question":"More visits ___ indicate interest, but do not prove accuracy.","options":["may","definitely"]},{"number":5,"question":"The entries ___ yesterday need review.","options":["added","adding"]},{"number":6,"question":"It is essential that errors ___ recorded.","options":["be","being"]},{"number":7,"question":"By Monday, staff will have ___ the section.","options":["check","checked"]},{"number":8,"question":"The claim must be consistent ___ the evidence.","options":["with","to"]},{"number":9,"question":"Only after approval ___ expansion begin.","options":["will","it will"]},{"number":10,"question":"The conclusion is limited ___ this section.","options":["to","at"]}]},"C":{"title":"C. Reading","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the passage and answer using evidence from the text. Each question is worth 4 marks.","passage":"Three accounts of a local archive project reach different conclusions. Attendance records show more visits after a digital catalogue was introduced. Interviews describe easier searching for some visitors, while a review of twelve record entries finds two unresolved errors. A draft report calls the catalogue an unqualified success and proposes discarding the paper index. The editor rejects that conclusion. Increased use is not equivalent to reliable retrieval, and the sources answer different questions. The archive coordinator proposes digitising one further section while retaining the originals. Expansion will stop if the review finds unresolved mismatches in that section. The review team must define a mismatch before beginning so that the threshold is not adjusted to fit the result. By the next meeting, the team will have checked the new entries. The report will then distinguish the reversible trial from the later, harder-to-reverse disposal decision. Caution about disposal is compatible with a clear next action.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"What does the attendance source show?"},{"number":2,"question":"How many reviewed entries have unresolved errors?"},{"number":3,"question":"Why is unqualified success too strong?"},{"number":4,"question":"What must be defined before review begins?"},{"number":5,"question":"Why are trial expansion and disposal separated?"}]},"D":{"title":"D. Listening","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the questions for one minute. Your coach will read the passage live twice. Write short answers. Each question is worth 4 marks.","delivery":"coach-live","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"Who will publish the review?"},{"number":2,"question":"When will it be published?"},{"number":3,"question":"Who decides on wider expansion?"},{"number":4,"question":"Why was improvements will be implemented removed?"},{"number":5,"question":"Why are some details withheld?"}]},"E":{"title":"E. Writing","marks":20,"instruction":"Write a recommendation to the archive committee. Synthesize the three sources, explain the risk of the proposed conclusion, distinguish reversible from irreversible action and set out a justified next step.","wordMin":200,"wordMax":230,"rubric":[{"criterion":"Task completion and relevant detail","marks":5},{"criterion":"Organisation and connection","marks":5},{"criterion":"Vocabulary appropriate to purpose","marks":5},{"criterion":"Grammar and written accuracy","marks":5}]}}},"8":{"version":3,"level":8,"title":"General English \u2014 Level 8","durationMinutes":45,"totalMarks":100,"sourceFile":"Speak_Boldly_GE_8_Exam.pdf","instructions":"Work independently without a dictionary or coursebooks. Read each instruction carefully. This is a course achievement exam; it does not certify a CEFR level. Speaking is assessed separately by your instructor. All cases are fictional.","sections":{"A":{"title":"A. Vocabulary in meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose a word from the word bank for each definition. Use each word once. Each item is worth 2 marks.","wordBank":["inference","commensurable","divergence","portfolio","precision","credibility","steelman","redundancy","qualification","granularity"],"questions":[{"number":1,"question":"exactness in wording and meaning"},{"number":2,"question":"movement towards difference"},{"number":3,"question":"a limit placed on a claim"},{"number":4,"question":"a strong and fair reconstruction of an opposing argument"},{"number":5,"question":"a conclusion drawn from observed details"},{"number":6,"question":"the level of detail used"},{"number":7,"question":"a selected collection showing work and development"},{"number":8,"question":"unnecessary repetition"},{"number":9,"question":"capable of meaningful comparison"},{"number":10,"question":"the quality of being believable for good reasons"}]},"B":{"title":"B. Grammar and intended meaning","marks":20,"instruction":"Choose the correct option. Where a meaning is specified, choose the form that expresses that meaning. Each item is worth 2 marks.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"The condition depends ___ approval.","options":["on","of"]},{"number":2,"question":"The interviews are reported ___ describe ease of use.","options":["to","for"]},{"number":3,"question":"Earlier, staff had ___ a guarantee.","options":["publish","published"]},{"number":4,"question":"Even ___ the form helps, it cannot guarantee timing. (hypothetical)","options":["if","despite"]},{"number":5,"question":"The editor revised the first sentence and the second ___.","options":["one","ones"]},{"number":6,"question":"Requests ___ during the trial were reviewed.","options":["received","receiving"]},{"number":7,"question":"The task involves selecting, editing and ___.","options":["reflecting","reflection"]},{"number":8,"question":"Staff checked ___ the trial requests, no others.","options":["only","all"]},{"number":9,"question":"They should have ___ the scope.","options":["check","checked"]},{"number":10,"question":"What matters ___ the evidence.","options":["is","are"]}]},"C":{"title":"C. Reading","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the passage and answer using evidence from the text. Each question is worth 4 marks.","passage":"A regional service office publishes a guide saying that its new request form guarantees a reply within two days. The trial behind that statement involved ten requests: eight received a reply within two days and two took longer. A separate staff note records fewer clarification emails, while interviews with four applicants describe the form as easier to follow. The editor separates those outcomes rather than treating them as three proofs of the same claim. The office agrees to retract the guarantee. A proposed replacement says that replies may take longer, but the editor asks for the observed result as well, so that caution does not become vague. The revised guide states the trial figures and identifies the next action for applicants whose requests remain unanswered. A short public version and a longer explanatory note retain the same factual core. The longer note explains the trial\u2019s limitations; neither version claims that the form alone caused faster replies. The editorial rationale records why the universal claim changed and why the distinction between ease of use and response time remained.","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"What trial result contradicts the guarantee?"},{"number":2,"question":"Which two other outcomes appear in the sources?"},{"number":3,"question":"Why does may take longer alone not satisfy the editor?"},{"number":4,"question":"What must the short and long versions share?"},{"number":5,"question":"Which causal claim is avoided?"}]},"D":{"title":"D. Listening","marks":20,"instruction":"Read the questions for one minute. Your coach will read the passage live twice. Write short answers. Each question is worth 4 marks.","delivery":"coach-live","questions":[{"number":1,"question":"Which three text types must be included?"},{"number":2,"question":"What must accompany each final text?"},{"number":3,"question":"What three elements should commentary contain?"},{"number":4,"question":"What should at least one example retain?"},{"number":5,"question":"What does the transfer task require?"}]},"E":{"title":"E. Writing","marks":20,"instruction":"Write an editorial rationale for revising the service-office guide. Include an accurate replacement for the guarantee, distinguish the three source outcomes and explain how the short version can remain accessible without changing certainty or scope.","wordMin":200,"wordMax":230,"rubric":[{"criterion":"Task completion and relevant detail","marks":5},{"criterion":"Organisation and connection","marks":5},{"criterion":"Vocabulary appropriate to purpose","marks":5},{"criterion":"Grammar and written accuracy","marks":5}]}}}};

// Manual assignments/tests from Ask your coach → Submissions.
const SB_STUDENT_SUB_HEADERS=['Request ID','Received at (UTC)','Name','Reply email','Type','Subject','Message','Private attachments JSON','Fingerprint','Email status','Error'];
const SB_STUDENT_SUB_TYPES={pdf:'application/pdf',doc:'application/msword',docx:'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document',ppt:'application/vnd.ms-powerpoint',pptx:'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation',xls:'application/vnd.ms-excel',xlsx:'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet',txt:'text/plain',jpg:'image/jpeg',jpeg:'image/jpeg',png:'image/png',webp:'image/webp',gif:'image/gif',mp3:'audio/mpeg',wav:'audio/wav',m4a:'audio/mp4',ogg:'audio/ogg',mp4:'video/mp4',webm:'video/webm'};
function setupStudentSubmissions(){
 const book=sbExamBook(),props=PropertiesService.getScriptProperties();let sheet=book.getSheetByName('Student submissions');if(!sheet)sheet=book.insertSheet('Student submissions');if(!sheet.getLastRow()){sheet.appendRow(SB_STUDENT_SUB_HEADERS);sheet.setFrozenRows(1);}else if(JSON.stringify(sheet.getRange(1,1,1,11).getValues()[0])!==JSON.stringify(SB_STUDENT_SUB_HEADERS))throw Error('Submission headers differ. Existing data has not been replaced.');
 let id=props.getProperty('SB_STUDENT_SUBMISSIONS_FOLDER');if(id){if(DriveApp.getFolderById(id).isTrashed())throw Error('Restore the private submissions folder before continuing.');}else{const folder=DriveApp.createFolder('Speak Boldly — Private student submissions');folder.setSharing(DriveApp.Access.PRIVATE,DriveApp.Permission.NONE);id=folder.getId();props.setProperty('SB_STUDENT_SUBMISSIONS_FOLDER',id);}
 MailApp.getRemainingDailyQuota();props.setProperty('SB_STUDENT_SUBMISSIONS_ENABLED','true');console.log('Manual assignment/test submissions ready. New private folder and Student submissions sheet only; no client/session rows or signatures changed. Deploy a New version of the existing Clients web app.');
}
function sbStudentSubmission(data,requestSize){
 const json=x=>ContentService.createTextOutput(JSON.stringify(x)).setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON),lock=LockService.getScriptLock();
 try{
  const props=PropertiesService.getScriptProperties();if(props.getProperty('SB_STUDENT_SUBMISSIONS_ENABLED')!=='true')throw Error('Your coach needs to run setupStudentSubmissions and deploy the updated exam script.');
  if(requestSize>21000000)throw Error('Keep attachments within 15 MB total.');
  const requestId=String(data.requestId||''),name=String(data.name||'').trim(),email=String(data.email||'').trim().toLowerCase(),kind=String(data.kind||''),message=String(data.message||'').trim();
  if(data.website||! /^[a-zA-Z0-9-]{16,100}$/.test(requestId)||!name||name.length>100||/[\r\n]/.test(name)||! /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)||email.length>254||!['assignment','test'].includes(kind)||message.length>3900)throw Error('Check your name, email and submission type.');
  const files=sbStudentSubmissionFiles(data.attachments);if(!message&&!files.length)throw Error('Attach your work or write your answer before sending.');
  const subject=(kind==='test'?'Test':'Assignment')+' submission — '+name;
  const fingerprint=sbExamHash(JSON.stringify([name,email,kind,message,files.map(f=>[f.name,f.mimeType,f.bytes.length,Utilities.base64Encode(Utilities.computeDigest(Utilities.DigestAlgorithm.SHA_256,f.bytes))]) ]));
  lock.waitLock(20000);const sheet=sbExamBook().getSheetByName('Student submissions');if(!sheet)throw Error('Run setupStudentSubmissions first.');
  const rows=sheet.getLastRow()>1?sheet.getRange(2,1,sheet.getLastRow()-1,11).getValues():[],existing=rows.find(r=>String(r[0])===requestId);
  if(existing){if(String(existing[8])!==fingerprint)throw Error('This submission changed. Start a new submission.');if(existing[9]==='sent')return json({ok:true,status:'sent'});throw Error('Your submission is saved, but email delivery is not confirmed. Ask your coach to check Student submissions and Sent Mail before sending it again.');}
  const today=Utilities.formatDate(new Date(),'Africa/Cairo','yyyy-MM-dd'),daily=rows.filter(r=>Utilities.formatDate(new Date(r[1]),'Africa/Cairo','yyyy-MM-dd')===today);
  if(daily.length>=50||daily.filter(r=>String(r[3]).replace(/^'/,'')===email).length>=3)throw Error('The daily submission limit has been reached. Please try again tomorrow.');
  if(MailApp.getRemainingDailyQuota()<1)throw Error('Email is temporarily unavailable. Keep your files and try again later.');
  const folderId=props.getProperty('SB_STUDENT_SUBMISSIONS_FOLDER');if(!folderId)throw Error('Run setupStudentSubmissions first.');const folder=DriveApp.getFolderById(folderId);if(folder.isTrashed())throw Error('Your coach needs to restore the private submissions folder.');
  const row=sheet.getLastRow()+1,safe=v=>/^[=+\-@\t\r]/.test(v)?"'"+v:v;
  sheet.getRange(row,1,1,11).setValues([[requestId,new Date().toISOString(),safe(name),safe(email),kind,safe(subject),safe(message),'[]',fingerprint,'saving','']]);
  const attachments=[],stored=[];
  try{
   for(const f of files){const blob=Utilities.newBlob(f.bytes,f.mimeType,f.name),saved=folder.createFile(blob);attachments.push(blob);stored.push({id:saved.getId(),name:f.name,mimeType:f.mimeType,size:f.bytes.length});sheet.getRange(row,8).setValue(JSON.stringify(stored));}
   sheet.getRange(row,10,1,2).setValues([['sending','']]);SpreadsheetApp.flush();
   MailApp.sendEmail({to:'submissions@speakboldly.space',replyTo:email,name:'Speak Boldly',subject,attachments,body:(kind==='test'?'Test':'Assignment')+' submission\n\nName: '+name+'\nReply email: '+email+'\nSubmission ID: '+requestId+'\nAttachments: '+files.length+'\n\n'+(message||'(Work attached)')+'\n\nEnglish Language Coaching\n© 2026 Founded by Mira Nasser Louis.'});
   sheet.getRange(row,10,1,2).setValues([['sent','']]);return json({ok:true,status:'sent'});
  }catch(error){const status=String(sheet.getRange(row,10).getValues()[0][0])==='sending'?'delivery_unknown':'saved_incomplete';sheet.getRange(row,10,1,2).setValues([[status,String(error.message||error).slice(0,1000)]]);throw Error(status==='delivery_unknown'?'Your submission is saved, but email delivery is not confirmed. Ask your coach to check Student submissions and Sent Mail before sending it again.':'Your submission record is saved, but some attachments could not be stored. Keep your files and ask your coach to check the submission record before trying again.');}
 }catch(error){return json({ok:false,error:String(error.message||error)});}finally{if(lock.hasLock())lock.releaseLock();}
